Z||000005||N_Man||02-16-2001||08:34 PM||||well ive been thinking about this one and have abunch of reasons why i shouldnt get a ticket<P>a) cop didnt see me do anything<BR>b) ticket issued because of third party's statement<BR>c) Cop wasnt even sure it was the integra that spun tires<BR>d) i was behind the integra therefor cant have spun them<BR>e) the only thing the cop is sure of is that the integra was doing about 100 in a 70 zone<P>and i think its just descimination for driving a sports car<BR>but i think i have a solid statement to present in court.<P>heh the cop even told me the other guy had a bad attitude and that i should fight this...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shaun41178||02-16-2001||08:42 PM||||Show up to court.<P>plead not guilty.<P>You will probably have to go to a secondary hearing in front of a judge or something and the cop should be there as well.  Tell the judge that the officer didn't see you do anything and that the cop admitted he didn't see you do anything wrong.  if a cop didnt see you do it then he can't ticket you for it based on what was said by a third party.  Besides you could always tell the judge it wasn't you and that you must have been mistaken for someone else<P>What I want to know is how did the cop find you when he didn't even get your license plate?  And if he did, how when he was pulling the other guy over?<P>Fight it.  it will get taken off.  you won't have to pay a thing except for your time<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
